From: TNG Technical Manual compatibility investigation
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] DIRECTOR: Activate digital video assigned with setCast

Channel::setCast() loads and starts a newly assigned digital-video cast member,
but a paused-at-start member can leave the channel movie rate at zero. Director's
playback/wait logic then treats it as inactive and advances immediately.

Match the active rate established by the normal score-channel replacement path.
This restores corridor fly-through transit movies in Star Trek: The Next
Generation Interactive Technical Manual.
---
 engines/director/channel.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/engines/director/channel.cpp b/engines/director/channel.cpp
index b1032265..8788756c 100644
--- a/engines/director/channel.cpp
+++ b/engines/director/channel.cpp
@@ -496,6 +496,11 @@ void Channel::setCast(CastMemberID memberID) {
 			DigitalVideoCastMember *dv = (DigitalVideoCastMember *)_sprite->_cast;
 			if (dv->loadVideoFromCast()) {
 				_movieTime = 0;
+				// A cast member assigned to a sprite from Lingo is expected to
+				// begin playing.  In particular, paused-at-start QuickTime members
+				// otherwise leave the channel rate at zero, causing "wait for video"
+				// logic to consider the movie inactive and advance immediately.
+				_movieRate = 1.0;
 				dv->setChannel(this);
 				dv->startVideo();
 			}
